  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to accept an\napplication for a real property tax exemption from 786 Muhammadi Masjid, Inc.",
    "basePrintNo": "S7472",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7472-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7472\n\nSPONSOR: CANZONERI-FITZPATRICK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to\naccept an application for a real property tax exemption from 786 Muham-\nmadi Masjid, Inc.\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo grant a retroactive property tax exemption for the assessment roll\nfor all the 2019-2020 assessment roll for a portion of the 2020 general\ntaxes and the 2021-2022 and 2022-2023 assessment rolls for a portion of\nthe 2021-2022 and 2022-2023 school taxes and all of the 2022 and 2023\ngeneral taxes for the parcel owned by such not-for-profit corporation\nlocated at 704 Doblin Street, hamlet of Elmont, town of Hempstead, coun-\nty of Nassau, otherwise known as Nassau county tax map district section\n37 block 653 lot 23.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Sets forth the authorization of Nassau County to accept the\nreal property tax exemption for certain property from 786 Muhammadi\nMasjid, Inc.\n\nSection 2. Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Muhammadi Masjid is a not-for-profit, tax-exempt religious organiza-\ntion. Allowing the organization to be forgiven of these property tax\nbills will allow them to continue their work in the community and keep\ntheir place of worship. This legislation would allow for the Nassau\nCounty Assessor to accept an application for a retroactive property tax\nexemption for the Muhammadi Masjid and therefore, would relieve the\ncurrent fiscal burden on this organization.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
